above at runtime via a separate child JVM (for the decompilers) or
directly (for ASM, SLF4J, Logback, JavaFX). The licenses of all bundled
dependencies permit such linking with GPL-3.0-licensed works, subject
to the following notes:

  * JavaFX is licensed under GPL-2.0 + Classpath Exception, which
    explicitly permits dynamic linking with code under any license.
  * ASM (BSD-3-Clause), CFR (MIT), Quiltflower (Apache-2.0),
    Vineflower (Apache-2.0), and SLF4J (MIT) are permissive licenses
    that allow combination with GPL-3.0 works.
  * Logback is dual-licensed under EPL-1.0 OR LGPL-2.1; both licenses
    permit linking with GPL-3.0 code (the LGPL-2.1 explicitly allows
    dynamic linking with non-LGPL code).

Sources for the bundled jars
----------------------------

All jars were obtained from Maven Central (https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/)
with the exception of the JavaFX Linux jars, which come from
org.openjfx:javafx-*-linux Maven Central artifacts.

The Quiltflower 1.9.0 jar is included as the runtime fallback for the
"Fernflower" combo box entry. Users who want the very latest JetBrains
Fernflower build can drop a manually-obtained `fernflower*.jar` into
the `../lib/` directory; the `DecompilerLocator` will pick it up at
runtime in preference to Quiltflower.
